{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on c9154743 for the cutover head (05d618e2).\n\n6. Choose (b). Change `platform:inbox@1` in place, and add no\n`@2`. The rule's logic is the same: it records the fact that the\ndelivery came from. Format word 2 gives every fact reference its\nnew shape, and this record follows it. A rule takes a new version\nwhen its logic changes. The three changes of the family plan\n(9ecd3efa) are the first such changes. Choice (a) keeps a rule that\nno room of this code line can run, because no reference has `inc`.\nThe reader commit keeps the old rule for the retired rooms.\n\nMove `D1_FACT` at destination.ts:3029 to genesis in the same way.\n\nThe declared data of both definitions changes, so their digests\nchange. Recompute each pin that the change reaches, in this head.\nList each old digest and its new digest in the implementation\nnote. For a cohort in native-catalog.ts that no creation path\nselects after the cutover, you may delete the cohort and its tests\nin place of the recomputation, when that is the smaller change.\nEvery room of such a cohort retires at the cutover (c0a795e7).\nName each deleted cohort in the review request.\n\nThis ruling also answers one item of 9ecd3efa: the cutover head\nforces new digests where declared data states a reference, and it\nforces no new rule version.\n\n7. Confirmed, all four. A kind that a message body states is a\nword that the sender wrote. It proves nothing, and ruling 3 of\n080e7c84 covers it. Drop the kind part of the checks on\n`body[\"directory\"]`, `fields[\"destination\"]` and\n`body[\"membership\"]`, and keep each `isScopeRef` shape check. The\nrules-creator check reads `made.sourceKind`, which the Directory's\nown entry records under b02334db. Remove the three QUESTION\ncomments. Where the next line compares one of these references\nwith a caller's place or with an admitted row, keep the comparison.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}